# Full deck pass

A new commander (no list yet) or a deck to evaluate (paste, file, Moxfield, Archidekt, MTGO) runs the whole pass. One lookup is not the pass. If a named tool is missing, say so and stop. Do not fill the gap from memory.

Every build runs both schools on the same list. NeRo picks the bend, the win, and the cards that do a job the turn you cast them. Defcat then asks when in the turn that card wants to resolve, and whether casting it makes another card better. A card that fails either school is out.

## New commander

`get_skill` and follow it. Do not skip a skill because the commander looks obvious.

1. `deckbuilding_principles`, then `get_skill("nero-build")`. That skill is the order, including the Defcat steps.
2. `reference_principles(source="nero")`, `get_card` the commander, `reference_deck`. A hit starts from his list and switches to the evaluate pass. Do not brew a second one.
3. `get_skill("nero-read")`, then `get_skill("defcat-read")`. `get_card_rulings` when the ability uses X, "this turn", "each turn", or a timing word. `Bar: none` is a complete answer when the commander does not compare mana value.
4. `get_skill("nero-lines")`. `search_combos` or `search_cards` as that skill says. A one-spell or edict-pile win does not get a combo package.
5. `get_skill("nero-hunt")`, then `get_skill("defcat-turn")` on those keeps. `get_skill("defcat-fuel")` only when the bar is real. A fuel card still has to do a NeRo job the turn you cast it.
6. `get_skill("nero-mana")` on the finished list.
7. `analyze_deck`, `price_decklist`, `find_combos`, `get_skill("nero-goldfish")`. Re-price before telling anyone to buy.
8. After the list exists: `edhrec_recommendations` with `budget="budget"`, and `archidekt_popular_cards`. Both show the shell. Neither is the shopping list.

## Evaluate a list

Get the list as text first. `archidekt_get_deck` for an Archidekt URL. Then `get_skill("nero-tune")` and follow it: `analyze_deck`, `price_decklist`, `get_card`, `reference_deck`, `find_combos`, `reference_compare`, the goldfish skill, and the mana skill when one color's pips sit well above its sources. A new card uses `nero-hunt`, then `defcat-turn`. A new line uses `nero-lines`. `defcat-read` on the commander. `defcat-fuel` only when that skill's bar is real.

`get_card` before you name an add or a cut. `get_card_rulings` if the line depends on timing. `get_card_printings` before telling anyone which copy to buy.

## Use the tool that owns the fact

Do not stop after the first tool that returns.

- Text, price, legality, roles: `get_card`. Speed: `simulate_deck`. Tested lists and staples: `reference_deck`, `reference_cards`, `reference_compare`, `reference_card`.
- Combos already in the list: `find_combos`. Combos to consider: `search_combos`.

Hand back the block the skill asks for. A new list leads with the bend, the turn, and the bar. An existing list leads with the one swap.

Example: "Build a $100 Rowan" runs steps 1–8. Her bar is none, so fuel is skipped and the turn check still runs. A pasted list runs the evaluate pass. Neither stops after `get_card`.
